@@text Not run. Built 2026-11-04, NOT installed. Targets `creativecommon-1.0.0.jar` (replaces `creativeengineering-1.1.09.jar`),
@@text `creativeengineering-2.0.0.jar` (new) and every Creative jar rebuilt against them (Compat, Calendar, Devtools, Delight,
@@text Brewing, Worldgen, Magic, Equipment: each now requires `creativecommon`). The 1.1.09 jars can no longer be rebuilt from the
@@text tree, so SQ-CMG and SQ-CEQ run on these jars too: read their `creativeengineering-common.toml` checks as "the carried
@@text tables are not in the Common or Engineering file". One save carried across: boot 1 on the jars in `mods/` today (1.1.09,
@@text Magic, Equipment); in the world: an IE sawmill with a precision sawblade cutting logs, a chest with a wooden water bucket,
@@text creosote-soaked sawdust and a precision sawblade, a dragon head facing away from an encased fan, a framed block with camo,
@@text an asphalt path; before boot 1 set `[shrapnel] count = 12`, `[surface.wthit] format = "PERCENT"`, `[toasts]` or `[jei]` one
@@text non-default value, and make sure `creativeengineering-swaps.toml` exists; `/save-all`; boot 2 on the new jars with no
@@text `creativecommon-common.toml`. Recipe and registry dumps from both boots (`/dumpall`) for the diffs.
