## SQ-CEN-01 | Common 1.1.0 and Engineering 2.0.0 load; every jar finds creativecommon; mixins apply
@group A
@commands Boot 2: mod list; `grep -E "creativecommon.mixins.json\|creativeengineering.mixins.json\|in both module\|split package" logs/latest.log`; `grep -c "from creativecommon.mixins.json" logs/debug.log`, same for `creativeengineering`
@pass Server boots; `creativecommon` 1.0.0 and `creativeengineering` 2.0.0 in the list, no other jar missing its `creativecommon` dependency; Common's 74 and Engineering's 29 mixins apply (gated ones with their mod), no apply error
@fails a jar still requires `creativeengineering [1.1.09,)`; package overlap between two jars; a gate id wrong (`EngineeringMixinPlugin`)
@from batches/r1113/c2_a1.qb
bootreject Missing or unsupported mandatory dependencies
bootreject (creativecommon|creativeengineering)\.mixins\.json.*(rror|ailed|could not)
bootreject in both module|split package
shell grep -oE "creative[a-z]+-[0-9.]+\.jar" logs/latest.log | sort -u | tr '\n' ' '; echo; grep -cE "from (mixins\.)?creativecommon\.mixins\.json" logs/debug.log; grep -cE "from (mixins\.)?creativeengineering\.mixins\.json" logs/debug.log; true
look jar list has creativecommon-1.1.0 and creativeengineering-2.0.0 (row said 1.0.0: Common is 1.1.0 since 2026-11-06); mixing counts: Common up to 46 common mixins, Engineering up to 17 (row's 74 / 29 predate later moves out); no apply error

## SQ-CEN-02 | Common's tables and the swaps file carried; interface tables reach Compat; values kept
@group A
@commands Same boot: read `config/creativecommon-common.toml`, `creativeengineering-common.toml`, `creativecommon-swaps.toml`; restart, read again
@pass Log `[swaps] config sections ... carried over` into `creativecommon-common.toml`; the edited `[toasts]`/`[jei]` value is there; `creativeengineering-swaps.toml` renamed to `creativecommon-swaps.toml`; after the restart the CE file holds only `[shrapnel]` (count 12), `[surface]` (format PERCENT) and `[vein_undo]`
@fails `CommonConfig.SECTIONS` incomplete; carry ran after Forge read the file
@from batches/r1113/c2_l1.qb
bootexpect \[swaps\] config sections \[changelog, damage_tags, perf, wandering_trader, advancements, mod_names\] carried over from creativeengineering-common.toml to creativecommon-common.toml
bootexpect \[swaps\] config creativeengineering-swaps.toml carried over to creativecommon-swaps.toml
bootexpect \[swaps\] config sections \[leaf_piles, moss, vine_shearing, monster_box, trash_slot\] carried over from creativeengineering-common.toml to creativecompat-common.toml
bootexpect \[swaps\] config sections \[shrapnel, surface, vein_undo\] merged from creativeengineering-common.toml into creativecompat-common.toml
bootexpect \[swaps\] config sections \[jei, gui_title, toasts, tooltips, coaster, wthit\] merged from creativeengineering-common.toml into creativecompat-common.toml
shell ls config | grep -E "^creative"; grep -nE "^\s*count *=" config/creativecompat-common.toml | head -2; grep -nE "^\s*format *=" config/creativecompat-common.toml | head -3; grep -nE "^\s*tutorial *=" config/creativecompat-common.toml
look counts: shrapnel count = 12, [surface.wthit] format = "PERCENT", [toasts] tutorial = true in Compat's file; creativecommon-swaps.toml exists. Superseded parts of the row text: [toasts]/[jei] and [shrapnel]/[surface]/[vein_undo] now end in creativecompat-common.toml (moved 2026-11-06 / 2026-11-07), not in Common's or Engineering's file; Engineering 2.0.0 has no config of its own

## SQ-CEN-03 | startup packs: creativecommon first, then the pack folder, then the jars; no global.CEN missing
@group A
@commands Same boot: `grep -E "startup script packs in order\|global.CEN missing\|in any registered config" logs/kubejs/startup.log logs/kubejs/server.log`; registry dump diff (items, blocks) boot 1 vs boot 2
@pass Packs: `creativecommon` first, then the pack folder, then the jars (`creativeengineering` among them); no `global.CEN missing`, no NCH.cfg section miss; same item and block ids (components, coils, plates, dust piles, misc parts, wood pellets, amethyst dust and lens, every transition item)
@fails `HELPERS_MOD_ID` not `creativecommon` (helpers load late, every jar script fails); Engineering startup pack not in the jar
@from batches/r1113/c2_a1.qb
@reviewed 2026-11-16
shell grep -nE "startup script packs in order|global\.CEN missing|in any registered config" logs/kubejs/startup.log logs/kubejs/server.log | head -10 | cut -c1-300
> cdevtest reg item ^creativeengineering: max=1
> cdevtest reg block ^creativeengineering: max=1
waitlog \[cdevtest\] verb=reg kind=block regex=\S+ n= 20
expect \[cdevtest\] verb=reg kind=item regex=\S+ n=[1-9]\d*
reject \[cdevtest\] .*(done=0|error=)
shell python3 -c "import json;print('exported creativeengineering items', len(json.load(open('$INST/kubejs/exported/items_by_mod/creativeengineering.json'))['items']))"
kjsreject global\.CEN missing
look packs order creativecommon, then the pack folder, then the jars with creativeengineering among them; live item count (the `verb=reg kind=item ... n=` line) equals the exported (2026-11-10) count (the row's boot-1 diff against 1.1.09 is not possible: no 1.1.09 jar left; this compares with the last dump instead)

## SQ-CEN-04 | sawmill recipe ids unchanged; no purged-wood outputs
@group A
@commands Recipe dump diff boot 1 vs boot 2: ids under `creativeengineering:`, count of `creativeengineering:sawmill/` recipes; JEI-free check that no recipe outputs a removed wood item (`global.removedWoods` outputs)
@pass Same recipe ids and count (moved scripts keep NCH's default namespace); 211 jar sawmill recipes plus the pack's 5; no purged-wood output and no duplicate oak-twin recipes
@fails an Engineering script failed (server.log); `removed_woods.js` order vs `item_merges.js`
@from batches/r1113/c2_a1.qb
@reviewed 2026-11-16
> cdevtest recipes creativeengineering:sawmill/ max=500
waitlog \[cdevtest\] verb=recipes text=creativeengineering:sawmill/ n= 30
expect \[cdevtest\] verb=recipes text=creativeengineering:sawmill/ n=216 
reject \[cdevtest\] .*(done=0|error=)
shell grep -cE "^creativeengineering:sawmill/" $INST/kubejs/exported/recipes/all.csv; true
look 216 = 211 jar + 5 pack (and = the 2026-11-10 dump count from the shell line); removed-wood output check: no `verb=recipes` line outputs a removed wood item (global.removedWoods; max=500 lists them all)

## SQ-CEN-05
@group A
@commands Same save: `/data get block` the chest; `/summon minecraft:tnt ~ ~ ~ {Fuse:1}` near the bot, then `/execute if entity @e[type=creativeengineering:shrapnel]` count over 5 ticks
@pass Wooden water bucket, sawblade and sawdust keep their ids and NBT; 12 shrapnel pieces per TNT
@fails Engineering registries not created (`CreativeEngineering` constructor); config not read
@reviewed 2026-11-16
> forceload add 0 0 15 15
> fill 0 -60 0 15 -50 15 minecraft:air
> summon minecraft:tnt 8 -60 8 {Fuse:1}
> cdevtest tickwarp 3
waitlog \[cdevtest\] verb=tickwarp end=done ticks=3 30
> cdevtest entities 8 -60 8 24 type=creativeengineering:shrapnel
waitlog \[cdevtest\] verb=entities done= 30
expect \[cdevtest\] verb=entities n=12 
> kill @e[type=creativeengineering:shrapnel]
> forceload remove 0 0 15 15
reject \[cdevtest\] .*(done=0|error=)
look the carried chest (boot 1 save): `cdevtest inv X Y Z` at its position shows the wooden water bucket, sawblade and sawdust with their ids and NBT kept (position from the save prep)
